", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Present Continuous tense is used to talk about an action that is happening or in progress at the moment. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use Present Continuous tense, you can use contractions. You use them often in speaking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u2018It is heartwarming' </span> becomes <span class=\"italic\">\u2018It's heartwarming'.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u2018I am getting'  </span>becomes<span class=\"italic\"> \u2018I'm getting'.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u2018You are staying' </span>becomes<span class=\"italic\"> \u2018You're staying'.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "These renovations <span class=\"strong\">are eating</span> a hole in my wallet!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "At least you <span class=\"strong\">are staying</span> at the Peter hotel rather than paying an exorbitant amount somewhere else!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " It<span class=\"strong\">'s heartwarming</span> when you can get your friends to help you, right Peter?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yup, and that's why I<span class=\"strong\">'m getting</span> you both to help me clean this apartment. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put away"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to save"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I had the foresight to put some money away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le01ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when we talk about repairing a house."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to eat a hole in my wallet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend more money than the person estimated "}, {"type":